      "writtenOn": "2016-07-29T17:36:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"setting enable to True\" is a bit misleading. Firstly, it *might* suggest that you can set it directly in the DB, which is not the case. But more to the point, \"True\" is a Python representation of a boolean, as opposed to \"true\", the JSON representation of a boolean, which is what the user would actually set if using the HTTP API manually. More likely though, they\u0027re going to set --enable or --disable through a command line client, so we really shouldn\u0027t be referring to specific API attributes in these docs -- it\u0027s just not user-friendly language.\n\n\n  If this feature is enabled and `[security_compliance]\n  lockout_duration` is not set, then users may be locked out\n  indefinitely until the user is explicitly enabled via the API.",
      "revId": "388e6c463a1b0d4cb6fd5c40185024a1b8d557f4",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
